      "problem": "Differentiate ${x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={x}^{3}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{′} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =({x}^{3})^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{x}^{3}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2})(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+({x}^{3})(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$",
